  "markdown": "3173310\n\n\nAmerican Consular Service\nat ... RIGA, LATVIA.\n\n\nQUOTA\nImmigration Visa\n\n\n[ ] Nonpreference \n[x] Preference \n\nPassport No. 31014  / 585822  , issued by Soviet \n\nauthorities, Kiev, Russia\n\n\non the 20th\n\n\nday of December , A. D. 1926 , valid\nuntil the 30th day of January ,\nA. D. 1928\n\n<figure type=\"PHOTOGRAPH\">\n\n<description>A black-and-white portrait photograph of an elderly woman wearing a headscarf. A horizontal strip of paper is superimposed across the center of the image with the handwritten name 'Basia X Chlourman' written on it. In the upper right corner, there is a circular stamped impression. At the very bottom, centered text reads: '1-1095 GOVERNMENT PRINTING OFFICE'.</description></figure>\n\nNo. 840\n\nRussian Russian \n(Quota.) (Nationality.) \n\nDate: February 2nd, 1927\nFor the journey to the\nUnited States.\n\nSEEN:\nThe Bearer. Basia CHTOURMAN , who\n(Ternoff Schturman)\nRussian\nnationality, having\nis of\nis of\n(Citizen or subject.)\nbeen seen and examined, is classified as a Quota Immi-\ngrant and is granted this Immigration Visa, pursuant\nto the Immigration Act of 1924.\nThe validity of this Immigration Visa expires on\n\n\nthe 2nd day of June \n\n[STAMPED]\nAMERICAN CONSULAR SERVICE A: D. 1927 AMERICAN CONSULAR SERVICE FEE STAMP\n\n\n[SIGNED]\nH. C. W.\nVice Consul\nUnited States of America\n\n\n<figure type=\"PHOTOGRAPH\">\n\n<description>A black and white photograph of an official document, likely a portion of an immigration visa, featuring a serrated circular seal or stamp attached by a ribbon. The document text is partially visible.</description>Fee $9.00\nFee No. 284\n\nNOTE: This Immigration Visa will not entitle the person to whom issued to enter the United States if upon arrival in the United States, he is found to be inadmissible to the United States under the Immigration Laws. (Subdivision (g), Section 2, Immigration Act of 1924.)\n* Check appropriate classification</figure>\n\n<!